checks: Run-time checks

The generated C++ checks what Go checks, with Go's messages and exit code 2: an index of a
string, slice or array, a slice expression, a nil pointer dereference (*p, p.f, a value
method through a nil pointer), a call of a nil func value, a method call on a nil interface,
a failed type assertion, integer division by zero, and a negative shift count.

Most checks are in the runtime types, not in the generated code: gp::slice::operator[]
checks the index, gp::ptr::operator* checks for nil. gocpp build -nochecks defines
GOCPP_NOCHECKS, which turns off the bounds and nil checks (an index out of range is then
undefined behavior, as in C++). Division by zero and negative shifts keep their checks,
because C++ has undefined behavior there and the checks cost little. The panics that are
part of an operation (a write to a nil map, make with a bad length, append's overflow) stay
too.

A division by a constant that is neither 0 nor -1 is the plain C++ operator: nothing can go
wrong, so nothing is checked. gocpp emit -annotate -nochecks writes the annotations for a
program built with -nochecks.

Specification: docs/spec/cpp-mapping.md#runtime-checks-and-panics
See also: gocpp explain panics, gocpp explain interfaces
Also known as: check, nochecks, bounds, nil

Example (checks.gp):

    package main

    import "fmt"

    type node struct{ next *node }

    func main() {
    	xs := []int{1, 2, 3}
    	i := len(xs) - 1
    	n := &node{}
    	m := n.next
    	fmt.Println(xs[i], xs[1]/i, 10/3, m == nil, 1<<i)
    }

The C++ that gocpp emit -annotate writes for it:

    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #pragma once
    #include <gocpp/rt.hpp>

    namespace gpkg_main {
    struct node;

    struct node {
        gp::ptr<node> next;
        bool operator==(const node&) const = default;
        std::size_t gp_hash() const {
            return gp::hash_fields(next);
        }
        static constexpr auto gp_fields = gp::fields(gp::field(&node::next, "next", false, false));
    };
    static_assert(sizeof(node) == 16 && alignof(node) == 8);

    void main();

    } // namespace gpkg_main
    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/checks.gp.cpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/checks.gp.cpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #include "gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp"

    namespace gpkg_main {

    // ---- ./checks.gp:7: func main() {
    void main() {

    // ---- ./checks.gp:8: xs := []int{1, 2, 3}
        gp::slice<int64_t> xs = gp::slice_of<int64_t>({1, 2, 3});

    // ---- ./checks.gp:9: i := len(xs) - 1
        int64_t i = gp::len(xs) - 1;

    // ---- ./checks.gp:10: n := &node{}
    // gp[refcount] col 7: &T{...} allocates a new reference-counted box that holds the literal
    //     (gp::new_)
        gp::ptr<node> n = gp::new_<node>(node{});

    // ---- ./checks.gp:11: m := n.next
    // gp[checks] col 9: p.f through a pointer: -> on a gp::ptr checks for nil and panics like Go (gocpp
    //     build -nochecks removes it)
        gp::ptr<node> m = n->next;

    // ---- ./checks.gp:12: fmt.Println(xs[i], xs[1]/i, 10/3, m == nil, 1<<i)
    // gp[interfaces] col 2: fmt.Println: the runtime's gp::fmt functions take each operand with the
    //     descriptor of its Go type (gp::fmt::as), not boxed into an interface first (an operand of a
    //     non-pointer type with an Error method is, see the allocation note)
    // gp[order] col 14: gp_t0 holds a value that is read early: an operation that can panic must happen
    //     in Go's order, before the calls that come later in the statement
    // gp[checks] col 16: s[i] of a slice: gp::slice::operator[] checks the index and panics with Go's
    //     "index out of range" message (gocpp build -nochecks removes it)
    // gp[order] col 21: gp_t1 holds a value that is read early: an operation that can panic must happen
    //     in Go's order, before the calls that come later in the statement
    // gp[checks] col 23: s[i] of a slice: gp::slice::operator[] checks the index and panics with Go's
    //     "index out of range" message (gocpp build -nochecks removes it)
    // gp[checks] col 26: division of integers: gp::div panics for a zero divisor and gives Go's result
    //     for MIN / -1; these checks stay under -nochecks
    // gp[checks] col 49: shift by a count that is not a constant below the width: gp::shl panics for a
    //     negative count and gives Go's result for a count of the width or more; these checks stay
    //     under -nochecks
        { auto gp_t0 = xs[i]; auto gp_t1 = gp::div(xs[1], i); gp::fmt::Println(gp_t0, gp_t1, int64_t(3), m == nullptr, gp::shl(int64_t(1), i)); }

    // ---- ./checks.gp:13: }
    }

    } // namespace gpkg_main
